<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Solador per-host metrics agent: the unattended update LaunchAgent (#394).

  Generated by deploy/install.sh ONLY when run with its enable-timer flag
  (the flag's name cannot be written here: an XML comment may not contain two
  consecutive hyphens), from agent/deploy/app.solador.agent.update.plist,
  whose at-sign placeholders it renders (XML-escaped) into the paths it
  actually installed to. A re-run with the flag regenerates it; a re-run
  without the flag leaves it exactly as it is. A default install writes no
  updater at all.

  A SEPARATE job from the metrics LaunchAgent (app.solador.agent), in the same
  gui/<uid> domain, labelled <metrics label>.update. `solador-agent update`
  kickstarts the metrics service and then verifies it — and restores the
  previous binary if that fails — so it cannot run as that service: the
  restart would kill its own verifier. Nothing here is a LaunchDaemon and
  nothing runs as root; it runs as the user who opted in, inside that user's
  login session, and does not exist before anyone logs in.

  ProgramArguments is the same launcher the metrics service uses, with the
  same binary, env-file and log-file arguments, plus one more: the literal
  word `update`. In that mode the launcher does not export the env file at all
  — the updater reads it by itself, under EnvironmentFile= rules, and the
  token reaches exactly one place (the local health probe) — and it applies
  the scheduling guard described below before exec'ing `solador-agent update`.
  The token is in neither this plist nor the log.

  Cadence is the decision recorded on #394: DAILY, NO CATCH-UP. StartInterval
  is 24 h and there is no RunAtLoad, so loading this job fires nothing and the
  first check is a day later. launchd.plist(5) says a StartInterval firing
  that falls during sleep "will be missed"; StartCalendarInterval is the key
  that coalesces missed firings into one run at wake, which is exactly the
  behaviour this cadence forbids, and it is not used. The launcher's guard is
  what makes the property hold rather than the man page: it refuses to run
  `update` within five minutes of the last wake or boot (kern.waketime /
  kern.boottime), and within 23 h of the last attempt — exit 0 and a log
  line naming the reason; a discarded firing's next chance is a day later.
  A check the guard cannot place in time (an unreadable clock or stamp)
  is HELD with exit 6, a code the updater never uses, so it cannot read as
  a good day. Nothing here retries.

  EnvironmentVariables carries no secret. PATH is the SYSTEM directories and
  nothing else, narrower than the metrics service's: this job needs no
  container CLI, only launchctl and plutil (the updater) and sysctl, date,
  sed, head, tr, dirname, mv, rm and wc (the launcher's guard), all under
  /usr/bin, /bin, /usr/sbin or /sbin. /opt/homebrew/bin is group-writable by
  admin on a stock Homebrew install, and a process that reads the bearer
  token and renames a binary over the tailnet-facing service, unattended,
  once a day, must not resolve any command there. HOME is pinned to the directory every other path
  in this file was rendered under, because `solador-agent update` resolves
  the metrics install as ~/Library/LaunchAgents/<label>.plist under ITS HOME,
  and launchd's HOME is the user record's, not necessarily the installer's.
  SOLADOR_AGENT_LAUNCHD_LABEL names the metrics service this job maintains —
  its default value on a normal install, and the same seam the installer and
  the updater already honour for a throwaway label.

  ProcessType Background is right here and wrong for the metrics agent: this
  job has no timing-sensitive sampler, and the background QoS tier is where a
  once-a-day housekeeping process belongs.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>@LABEL@</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>@LAUNCHER@</string>
        <string>@BINARY@</string>
        <string>@ENV_FILE@</string>
        <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
        <string>update</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>@HOME@</string>
        <key>SOLADOR_AGENT_LAUNCHD_LABEL</key>
        <string>@METRICS_LABEL@</string>
    </dict>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>86400</integer>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
</dict>
</plist>
